# The foreign-only rescue licence, on the boxed shape. The chain's failure
# was raised by `mine`, in this file, and the `.?` is written in this file
# too, so the word hands it on without entering its callback and nothing
# downstream is foreign enough to end it: the program reaches the endpoint
# with it. Before the licence moved off the arm and onto the word (ruled
# 2026-09-15) the lambda was entered and this printed "claimed mine".
import "std/time"

fn mine _
  err "mine"

time/sleep 0 .> (_ -> mine 1) .? (e -> "claimed {e.reason}") .> print
